<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Static App Shortcuts (long-press the launcher icon).

     ONE static shortcut, on purpose. The launcher's long-press menu holds FOUR entries on the
     owner's phones, and it counts the shortcuts DECLARED HERE against that budget even when they
     are disabled at runtime — which is what the reader app learned the hard way (dg-apps
     adcd32d: "The launcher's long-press menu shows four entries in total, so four static shortcuts
     left room for two 'recently read' texts, not three"), and then forgot again when 3b08f69 put
     the four statics back and hid three with ShortcutManager.disableShortcuts(). The dictionary
     app had copied that second shape, and the owner counted the same two words out of three
     (2026-09-24: "он на самом деле пишет три.. но не показывает").

     So the whole other set is dynamic now, and DgShortcutsPlugin pushes whichever set the burger
     menu's switch asks for — the plugin no longer disables anything:

       switch OFF -> three programmed (Table of Contents, Dharmamitra, Aksharamukha), pushed here;
       switch ON  -> three recent words from the dictionary's own history;
       either way -> plus this one, which is the errand a reader returns to.

     Four entries in the menu, one of them declared and always present. Favorites & History is that
     one because it is the only one that belongs to BOTH sets, and because it is the only entry a
     reader sees on a freshly installed app, before it has ever run — a dynamic shortcut cannot
     exist before the app has run.

     Each shortcut starts MainActivity with a "route" extra, which MainActivity loads into the
     WebView. The dhamma.gift routes are in capacitor.config.json's server.allowNavigation, so they
     open inside this app exactly as they did inside the TWA; dharmamitra.org and aksharamukha.com
     are not, so those two open in the system browser (which is what a reader wants from an
     external tool anyway). -->
<shortcuts xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <shortcut
        android:shortcutId="favorites"
        android:enabled="true"
        android:icon="@drawable/shortcut_1"
        android:shortcutShortLabel="@string/shortcut_fav_short"
        android:shortcutLongLabel="@string/shortcut_fav_long">
        <intent
            android:action="android.intent.action.MAIN"
            android:targetPackage="gift.dhamma.pali"
            android:targetClass="gift.dhamma.pali.MainActivity">
            <extra android:name="route" android:value="https://dhamma.gift/4as" />
        </intent>
    </shortcut>
</shortcuts>
